---
title: "Motor Cortex — Plan, Build, Self-Check"
scope: global
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant TH as Thalamus
    participant EFF as Efference Copy
    participant SENS as Senses
    participant PRE as Premotor
    participant PRI as Primary
    participant MBC as Mid-Build
    participant PROP as Proprio
    participant EVAL as Eval

    Note over EFF: BEFORE consultation — <br/>predict what's actually buildable

    TH->>EFF: PNS capabilities + episodes + SOL
    EFF->>TH: Per-sense ceiling estimates,<br/>hard constraints, tension costs
    TH->>SENS: Efference copy in consultation briefing<br/>(senses adjust ambitions to reality)

    Note over PRE: PLAN the approach

    TH->>PRE: Motor briefing (task + consultation +<br/>SOL + capabilities + patterns)
    PRE->>PRE: Choose approach, detail steps,<br/>tension strategy, confidence

    Note over PRI: BUILD the artifact

    PRE->>PRI: Motor plan + tools (via PNS)
    loop Agentic building with real tools
        PRI->>PRI: Execute intention (read/write/shell)
        alt Hits ambiguity
            PRI->>MBC: BuildQuestion to specific sense
            MBC->>PRI: Targeted answer
        end
    end

    Note over PROP: SELF-CHECK (if NE ≥ 0.3)

    PRI->>PROP: Plan + built artifact
    PROP->>PROP: Plan adherence? Drift areas?<br/>Uncertainties? Suggested focus?
    PROP->>EVAL: Self-assessment guides<br/>where evaluators should look

    Note over PRE,EVAL: On revision: premotor re-plans<br/>with evaluation feedback,<br/>distinguishing execution-error<br/>(fix details) from plan-error<br/>(different approach entirely)
